# Pages and assets

## Pages

```yaml
---
layout: page
title: Visible title
permalink: /the-slug/
---
```

- Put lists in `_data/` and loop them (`documents.yml`, `galleries.yml`). Don’t copy a new HTML file per album or PDF.
- Use `{{ '/path/' | relative_url }}` and `{{ '/assets/…' | relative_url }}`.
- Shared chrome: `_includes/` (header, footer, gallery, donate, jotform). Restyle in `assets/main.scss` after `@import "minima"`.
- Keep `/compose/` and `/update/` out of `header_pages`. Form contracts: `officer-forms.mdc`.

## Assets

- GitHub Pages limits: ~1 GB repo, **100 MB per file**. Compress photos and PDFs before commit.
- Post / Instagram images: JPEG under `assets/images/posts/` (see Instagram post rule).
- Documents: PDF in `assets/documents/` + a row in `_data/documents.yml`.
- Don’t hotlink PhotoPrism originals as `image:` front matter or as the only copy of a news photo.

## GitHub Pages extras to prefer

- `jekyll-sitemap` and `jekyll-redirect-from` (whitelist) when adding SEO or old-URL redirects.
- `404.html` at the site root if adding a not-found page.
- Logo, default social image, and page `description:` — see `site-seo.mdc`.
